ustice  does the Probation Service have the  powers and resources to properly  supervise people who are clearly  dangerous and I think these questions  will be asked about this individual to  make sure we find out what happened here  but also there are wide lessons as well  yeah I would say if we move it away from  that individual for obvious reasons when  someone has been convicted of a of  a terror attack and they are released on  licence without having to go I mean  should it be automatic do you think that  someone under those circumstances  convicted of such a crime should  actually have to go before the parole  board before getting released yeah I  don't think that it's right that  somebody's convicted of a serious  offense like what this man was convicted  of should be automatically released in  fact I was somebody who voted against  the government getting rid of the IPP  sentence I think it's really important  for judges to have all the tools at  their disposal better people have heard  the evidence well let's find out what  happened this particular case but also I  believe of course people need to be  released if they've been rehabilitated  but that is we probably supervised with  the system that is effective that are  the proper resources and that's how you  keep the public confident that the  authorities are doing all that they can  to keep us safe  are you comfortable that the threat  level was reduced just a week or so ago  I am we've got a fantastic system in  that country where politicians don't  interfere with the Joint Terrorism  analysis centre who do the expert  analysis about threat levels arising  from international terrorism and just to  reassure your viewers the threat level  used to be severe which means that  attack is highly likely it was changed  to substantial which means an attack is  likely as far as the police are  concerned the Security Service are  concerned in my experiences the mayor  nothing changed the vigilance was still  there t